\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces v13 TrajDiff architecture (planned; not yet implemented). A bidirectional DiT denoises a 128-point noisy trajectory in normalised lon/lat space, conditioning on the same 163-token retrieval bank used by v10 (cross-attention) and on multi-scale SDF features sampled at the noisy positions (concatenated with the time embedding). At sample time, 8 trajectories are drawn in parallel, ranked by distance to the retrieval-top-1 neighbour minus a penalty for land crossings, and the best returned. The conditioning encoder (top) is reused verbatim from v10 (Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:v10-arch}), so the v10 retrieval substrate transfers into the diffusion setting without re-training the encoder.\relax }}{29}{figure.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v13-arch}{{17}{29}{v13 TrajDiff architecture (planned; not yet implemented). A bidirectional DiT denoises a 128-point noisy trajectory in normalised lon/lat space, conditioning on the same 163-token retrieval bank used by v10 (cross-attention) and on multi-scale SDF features sampled at the noisy positions (concatenated with the time embedding). At sample time, 8 trajectories are drawn in parallel, ranked by distance to the retrieval-top-1 neighbour minus a penalty for land crossings, and the best returned. The conditioning encoder (top) is reused verbatim from v10 (Figure~\ref {fig:v10-arch}), so the v10 retrieval substrate transfers into the diffusion setting without re-training the encoder.\relax }{figure.caption.27}{}}
